{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QtnhgLWD5TJc3go7ppnZt7","type":"tool_result","content":"50\t//!    ```\n51\t//!\n52\t//!    Standard top-down splay over `u32` indices.  Every \"follow a\n53\t//!    pointer\" in the C body becomes \"index into `self.slots`.\"\n54\t//!\n55\t//! 2. **Replace with a third-party crate.**  `splay_tree`,\n56\t//!    `splay-tree`, or BTreeMap (if log-N is fine and we don't\n57\t//!    actually need access locality).  picoquic uses splay\n58\t//!    specifically for the access-locality property in\n59\t//!    `connection_wake_tree` (the next-to-fire connection is usually the\n60\t//!    one we just touched).  `BTreeMap` is the safe-default\n61\t//!    fallback; a real splay crate is the performance-preserving\n62\t//!    choice.\n63\t//!\n64\t//! ## Phase 4 plan — call sites\n65\t//!\n66\t//! Same pattern as the hash table.  Every C site of the form\n67\t//!\n68\t//! ```c\n69\t//! struct Foo { …; picosplay_node_t node; …; };\n70\t//! picosplay_init_tree(&tree, foo_compare, foo_create, foo_delete, foo_value);\n71\t//! picosplay_insert(&tree, &foo);     // value = pointer to parent\n72\t//! ```\n73\t//!\n74\t//! becomes\n75\t//!\n76\t//! ```ignore\n77\t//! struct Foo {\n78\t//!     // … real fields …\n79\t//!     wake_tree_membership: Option<SplayToken>,   // for fast O(1) removal\n80\t//! }\n81\t//! let tok = tree.insert(key, foo_arena_token);\n82\t//! foo.wake_tree_membership = Some(tok);\n83\t//! // …\n84\t//! tree.remove(foo.wake_tree_membership.take().unwrap());\n85\t//! ```\n86\t//!\n87\t//! In particular, every C `_create` callback (which just projected\n88\t//! the embedded `SplayNode` out of a parent pointer) disappears —\n89\t//! the parent already lives in its own arena, the splay tree only\n90\t//! stores a token to it.\n91\t\n92\tuse core::marker::PhantomData;\n93\t\n94\tuse crate::Error;\n95\t\n96\t/// Opaque handle into a [`SplayTree`]'s slot vector.\n97\t///\n98\t/// `idx` selects a slot; `generation` is incremented on every\n99\t/// removal so an old token comparing against a recycled slot\n100\t/// returns `None` from [`SplayTree::get`].\n101\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, Eq, PartialEq, Hash)]\n102\tpub struct SplayToken {\n103\t    idx: u32,\n104\t    generation: u32,\n105\t}\n106\t\n107\t/// Splay tree mapping `K` to `V`, addressable by [`SplayToken`].\n108\t///\n109\t/// Operations rotate the touched node to the root for access"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c7c7e82c-a907-4d1f-a2c6-fbe9ac637b5e","uuid":"994f01d9-ec72-44fd-9ccf-27a82d2cd97c","timestamp":"2026-05-04T18:28:52.164Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/splay.rs","content":"//!    ```\n//!\n//!    Standard top-down splay over `u32` indices.  Every \"follow a\n//!    pointer\" in the C body becomes \"index into `self.slots`.\"\n//!\n//! 2. **Replace with a third-party crate.**  `splay_tree`,\n//!    `splay-tree`, or BTreeMap (if log-N is fine and we don't\n//!    actually need access locality).  picoquic uses splay\n//!    specifically for the access-locality property in\n//!    `connection_wake_tree` (the next-to-fire connection is usually the\n//!    one we just touched).  `BTreeMap` is the safe-default\n//!    fallback; a real splay crate is the performance-preserving\n//!    choice.\n//!\n//! ## Phase 4 plan — call sites\n//!\n//! Same pattern as the hash table.  Every C site of the form\n//!\n//! ```c\n//! struct Foo { …; picosplay_node_t node; …; };\n//! picosplay_init_tree(&tree, foo_compare, foo_create, foo_delete, foo_value);\n//! picosplay_insert(&tree, &foo);     // value = pointer to parent\n//! ```\n//!\n//! becomes\n//!\n//! ```ignore\n//! struct Foo {\n//!     // … real fields …\n//!     wake_tree_membership: Option<SplayToken>,   // for fast O(1) removal\n//! }\n//! let tok = tree.insert(key, foo_arena_token);\n//! foo.wake_tree_membership = Some(tok);\n//! // …\n//! tree.remove(foo.wake_tree_membership.take().unwrap());\n//! ```\n//!\n//! In particular, every C `_create` callback (which just projected\n//! the embedded `SplayNode` out of a parent pointer) disappears —\n//! the parent already lives in its own arena, the splay tree only\n//! stores a token to it.\n\nuse core::marker::PhantomData;\n\nuse crate::Error;\n\n/// Opaque handle into a [`SplayTree`]'s slot vector.\n///\n/// `idx` selects a slot; `generation` is incremented on every\n/// removal so an old token comparing against a recycled slot\n/// returns `None` from [`SplayTree::get`].\n#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, Eq, PartialEq, Hash)]\npub struct SplayToken {\n    idx: u32,\n    generation: u32,\n}\n\n/// Splay tree mapping `K` to `V`, addressable by [`SplayToken`].\n///\n/// Operations rotate the touched node to the root for access","numLines":60,"startLine":50,"totalLines":227}}}
